  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> 18</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="242" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ordal ⁊ aðas syndan tocweðen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.oe.1-3"/> freolsdagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ rihtymbrendagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ fram Adventu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> D<hi rend="italic">omi</hi>ni oð octabas Epiphanię ⁊ fram Septuagessimam oð XV niht ofer eastran.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-g2"><pb n="242" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ordal ⁊ aðos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.oe.1"/> syndan tocwedene freolsdagum ⁊ rihtymbrendagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> Aduentum D<hi rend="italic">omi</hi>ni oð octabas Epiphanige ⁊ fram Septuagessima oð XV niht ofer eastran.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="243" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ordol<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ⁊ aðas sindon tocweðen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.oe.2"/> freolsdagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ ymbrendagu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ ab Aduentu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> D<hi rend="italic">omi</hi>ni oð XIIII niht ofer middewintres tid ⁊ fram Septuages<hi rend="italic">ima</hi> oð XIIII niht ofer eastron.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="18" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="84" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ ordol ⁊ aðas sindon tocweðen<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.fn.6"/> freolsdagum ⁊ ymbrendagum<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.fn.7"/> ⁊ ab<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.fn.8"/> Adventum Domini oð XIIII niht ofer middewintres tid<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.fn.9"/> ⁊ fram Septuagesima oð XIIII<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.fn.10"/> niht ofer eastron.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="152" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ordal and aðas syndan tocweðen freolsdagum and rihtymbrendagum and fram Adventum Domini oð octabas Epiphanie and fram Septuagessiman oð XV niht ofer Eastran.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="243" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.1"/> Ordal und [gerichtliche] Eide sind untersagt an Festtagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.2"/> und gesetzlichen Quatembertagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.3"/> und von<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.4"/> Adventus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.5"/> Domini bis zur Octave Epiphaniae [13. Jan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.6"/>] (14<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.7"/> Tage nach Weihnachtsfest [8. Jan.] <hi rend="italic">D</hi>) und von Septuagesima<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.8"/> bis 14<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.9"/> Tage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#VAtr_18.lnote.de.10"/> nach Ostern.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And ordeals and [judicial] oaths are forbidden on feast-days and on the proper Ember days, and from Advent until the octave of Epiphany [13 January] (a fortnight after Christmas [8 January], D), and from Septuagesima until a fortnight after Easter.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="85" ed="#robertson"/>And trial by ordeal and [the rendering of] oaths are forbidden during festivals and on Ember days, and from the Advent<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.n.2"/> till a fortnight after Christmas<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.n.3"/>, and from the Septuagesima<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#VAtr_18.robnote.n.4"/> till a fortnight after Easter.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="450" ed="#whitelock"/>And ordeals and oaths<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_18.whinote.n.1"/> are forbidden on feast-days and the legal Ember days, and from the Advent of the Lord until the octave of Epiphany, and from Septuagesima until 15 days after Easter.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="153" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ordeals and oaths are prohibited during feasts and Ember Days and from Advent until the fourteenth night after midwinter and from the Septuagesima until the fifteenth night after Easter.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="243"><ref target="clause:EGu_9">EGu 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. E Gu. 9</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_25">VI Atr 25</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="58"><label>first appears in</label> <ref target="clause:EGu_9">EGu 9</ref> <quote>V Atr 18 – 20, VI Atr (Lat and OE) 25 – 25:2, Cn 1018 15 – 15:2. This point first appears in EGu 9</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="450"><label>expanded in</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_25">VI Atr 25</ref> <quote>VI Ethelred 25 adds “and weddings”</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘tocweðen’ should be corrected to ‘tocweden’ (G2). Liebermann compares EGu 9.; AY: corrected against Rabin p. 152 / 153, October 2026 (was “xiiii; xv: | xiiii”, now “XIIII; XV: XIIII”); AZ: corrected against Rabin p. 152 / 153, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “|”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">and fram: and ab D</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">octabas Epiphanie: XIIII niht ofer middewintres tid D XV: XIIII D</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Ember Days: Periods of fasting and prayer that take place during four weeks of the year (once during Lent and during the weeks of Pentecost, the Festival of the Exaltation of the Cross, and Saint Lucy’s Day) and consisting of the Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Septuagesima: The ninth Sunday before Easter.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">242</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">243</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so auch VI Atr.</hi> 25</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so also VI Atr. 25</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">243</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">242</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> tocweden <hi rend="italic">nach G 2</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read tocweden after G 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= VI 25 = (neben EGu) I Cn 17 = Hn 62, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= VI 25 = (alongside EGu) I Cn 17 = Hn 62, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Feiertag 8a; Quatember 3f.; Gerichtsferien 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Feiertag 8a; Quatember 3f.; Gerichtsferien 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Feiertag 8a; Quatember 3f.; Gerichtsferien 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Feiertag 8a; Quatember 3f.; Gerichtsferien 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hätte das Original mit D <hi rend="italic">ab</hi> gelesen, so stände <hi rend="italic">Adventu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Had the original read <hi rend="italic">ab</hi> with D, it would have <hi rend="italic">Adventu</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Advent; dieser und der folgende Zeitraum kehren wieder in Treuga Dei; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Advent; this period and the following one recur in the Treuga Dei; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diesen Hilarius-Tag beginnt Fehde wieder im 12. Jh.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the 12th cent. feud begins again on this day, St Hilary's day</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Termin D's begegnet sonst nicht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">D's date does not occur elsewhere</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Septuagesima</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Septuagesima</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sinn von GG 2 = D; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 11, 1³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sense of GG 2 = D; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 11, 1³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_18.lnote.de.10" n="10" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">173</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diesen Hilarius-Tag beginnt Fehde wieder im 12. Jh.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the 12th cent. feud begins again on this day, St Hilary's day</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_18.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. E. and G. 9; VI Atr. 25; I Cn. 17; Wulfstan, pp. 117, 208; <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg.</hi> 24, ed. Thorpe, <hi rend="italic">Anc. Laws</hi>, <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. p. 248.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_18.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the period preceding the festival of the Nativity, including the four preceding Sundays.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_18.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> January 8th.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_18.robnote.n.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> from the third Sunday before Lent.</seg></note>
